{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03073",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.83,
      "end_seconds": 5.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "Hello, um, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.21,
      "end_seconds": 10.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. Tell me why you came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.95,
      "end_seconds": 16.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "I've been dealing with bloating when I slip up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.59,
      "end_seconds": 25.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.18,
      "end_seconds": 40.17,
      "duration_seconds": 12.99,
      "text": "I've had it since this morning. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.55,
      "end_seconds": 51.89,
      "duration_seconds": 10.34,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.86,
      "end_seconds": 62.74,
      "duration_seconds": 8.88,
      "text": "it's worse with gluten. It settles a little with avoiding gluten. It feels mild to me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.05,
      "end_seconds": 66.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Right, is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.61,
      "end_seconds": 76.1,
      "duration_seconds": 8.49,
      "text": "It usually comes with a rash on my elbows. The rash on my elbows? That's been for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.04,
      "end_seconds": 81.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.9,
      "end_seconds": 85.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "um, I'd call it moderate"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.17,
      "end_seconds": 86.87,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.11,
      "end_seconds": 104.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "any diarrhoea or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.16,
      "end_seconds": 107.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.18,
      "end_seconds": 115.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "any vomiting or bone pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.68,
      "end_seconds": 123.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Yeah, no, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.87,
      "end_seconds": 126.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Ah. Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.49,
      "end_seconds": 131.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.74,
      "end_seconds": 135.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.87,
      "end_seconds": 138.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.24,
      "end_seconds": 143.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.79,
      "end_seconds": 163.66,
      "duration_seconds": 18.87,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner. I smoke roughly a pack every two days. I retired from the post office two years ago. I grab fast food at lunch most days. My husband and I live above the shop"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.97,
      "end_seconds": 170.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Okay, do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.54,
      "end_seconds": 174.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "no, I've never reacted to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.19,
      "end_seconds": 186.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.55,
      "end_seconds": 195.86,
      "duration_seconds": 8.31,
      "text": "Diabetes, for nearly five years. I've been reading about it online and it worried me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.75,
      "end_seconds": 200.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.09,
      "end_seconds": 211.56,
      "duration_seconds": 10.47,
      "text": "Glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar. Well, you know, I was on metformin before. I stopped taking it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.52,
      "end_seconds": 216.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "what operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.36,
      "end_seconds": 225.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Just an operation for a hernia, last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 235.33,
      "end_seconds": 243.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temperature is 36.7 degrees, BP is 118 over 74, heart rate 86."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.52,
      "end_seconds": 246.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Okay, good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.37,
      "end_seconds": 251.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Right, let's have a proper look at you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.59,
      "end_seconds": 254.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.02,
      "end_seconds": 277.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "your tummy is soft and your weight is stable on the scales"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.3,
      "end_seconds": 280.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.15,
      "end_seconds": 310.8,
      "duration_seconds": 26.65,
      "text": "You can relax now. Okay, thinking it through, it's hard to to say. Coeliac disease on a gluten-free diet with some accidental exposure is one possibility and iron deficiency another, and I'd rather not commit yet. Let's book a blood count to look into coeliac follow-up. One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.73,
      "end_seconds": 315.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}